{
 "note": "What is in each dungeon (core/game/game_dungeons.gd, checked by tools/check_data.gd). A dungeon's rooms have a `role` in spaces.json `rooms`; here each dungeon says, per role, who lives in such a room (`foes`: how many, from a weighted pool; a creature appears only in its own era, and the dungeon's `fallback` pool is used when none of the pool is of the era), what stands in it (`containers`: a kind and a loot tier from data/items/dungeon_loot.json), what is hidden in it (`traps`, from `traps` below) and `features` (a prop of the theme the heir can use: a shrine that heals, or an inscription). The lair boss of a dungeon is the creature world.json gives as its `lair`, put in its boss_lair room when it is stirring. Where things stand is worked out from the dungeon's id alone (the same every game); who is met and what is found use dice keyed on the seed, never the dynasty's. What the heir has opened, sprung, used or killed is saved in the dynasty's `dungeon_marks` (only once something is) and comes back after `refill_years` or `foe_years` of the world's calendar.",
